        "original_id": "838e9c98-0b43-578d-9a1c-d42886807975",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic\n- People: Jennifer Jones, Cathy Overton-Clapham, Jill Officer, Dawn Askin, Rachel Homan\n- Organizations: Women's World Curling Tour\n- Places: Calgary Curling Club, Calgary, Alberta, Sochi\n- Topics: curling championships, Grand Slam, prize purse\n\nFacts:\n- The 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic was the 30th annual edition of the event.\n- The 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic was the first Grand Slam event of the Women's World Curling Tour.\n- The 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic was held from October 5 to 9, 2007, at the Calgary Curling Club in Calgary, Alberta.\n- The 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic had a total purse of $56,000, and the winning team of Jennifer Jones, Cathy Overton-Clapham, Jill Officer, and Dawn Askin received $14,000.\n- Jennifer Jones and her team won the 2008 World Women's Curling Championship.\n- Rachel Homan became the next Canadian women's skip to win the World Women's Curling Championship in 2017 after Jennifer Jones's team in 2008.\n- Jennifer Jones won an Olympic gold medal as skip of the Canadian team at the 2014 Sochi Games.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5f3addd3-3b02-57cd-8152-a06b24d125a5",
        "text": "Page: 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic. Sentence: The 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic was the 30th annual edition of the event.\nPage: 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic. Sentence: It marked the first Grand Slam event of the Women's World Curling Tour.\nPage: 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic. Sentence: It was held October 5-9 at the Calgary Curling Club in Calgary, Alberta.\nPage: 2007 Trail Appliances Autumn Gold Curling Classic. Sentence: The total purse for the event was $56,000 with $14,000 going to the winning team of Jennifer Jones, Cathy Overton-Clapham, Jill Officer and Dawn Askin.\nPage: Jennifer Jones (curler). Sentence: She won an Olympic gold medal as skip of the Canadian team at the 2014 Sochi Games.\nPage: Jennifer Jones (curler). Sentence: They won the 2008 World Women's Curling Championship, and were the last Canadian women's team to do so until Rachel Homan in 2017.",
